      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Current Australian Antarctic activities require a unique medical service: a sole medical officer is responsible for the total care of 20 to 30 expeditioners (and of himself) for around nine months a year. A case of \"acute abdomen\" at Casey, Antarctica, is described and the problems of diagnosis and management, in this isolated medical practice, are discussed."},
